@program xim-test
@compositor kwin
@xwayland
@x11
# As xim-sway.keys, with KWin (which starts the daemon itself):
# An X11 application without a HIME module on Xwayland, with the daemon on
# Wayland (layer-shell, no X display of GDK's): it types through XIM, as on
# X11: the client sends keys once Control+Space (a trigger key) turned the
# input method on.  Shift types English; Control+Space turns it off and
# on.  A mouse action (as a click on the symbol table) commits to it
# directly, and virtual keyboard keys go through the engine.
a C-<space> b 1 a <space> @check S-h S-i C-<space> a C-<space> a <space> @check @hook commit 好 @check @hook key b @hook key 1
